WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.581
Conversation history helps resolve references such as that order, but it is

00:00:04.581 --> 00:00:06.490
not an authoritative business database.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:12.367
Separate recent message history, summaries, durable user preferences, and workflow state.

00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:15.278
Each has a different retention period and trust level.

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:19.257
A summary is a generated interpretation and may omit details needed for

00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:20.534
an approval or audit.

00:00:20.684 --> 00:00:25.766
Scope memory to authenticated users and tenants, limit its size, and support

00:00:25.766 --> 00:00:27.037
expiration and deletion.

00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:31.851
Avoid storing secrets or unnecessary personal information in prompts and logs.

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:37.849
Durable workflow state should record exact identifiers, versions, statuses, and completed effects

00:00:37.849 --> 00:00:41.260
rather than relying on a natural-language summary.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.635
A user asks about A100 and then says cancel it.

00:00:44.785 --> 00:00:49.545
The application must resolve it to the correct authorized order, fetch current

00:00:49.545 --> 00:00:51.529
state, and apply cancellation rules.

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:56.135
A memory entry saying user approved cancellation yesterday cannot authorize a new

00:00:56.135 --> 00:00:56.877
action today.

00:00:57.027 --> 00:01:00.959
The supplied engine keeps only one run’s bounded history and has no

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:01.614
cross-session memory.

00:01:01.764 --> 00:01:07.831
Design a memory record with tenant, user, conversation ID, creation time, expiry,

00:01:07.831 --> 00:01:08.842
and source.

00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:12.899
Write tests for two users with the same conversation ID in different

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:14.526
tenants and for expired entries.

00:01:14.676 --> 00:01:18.384
Use a composite namespace or equivalent authorization predicate.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:21.654
Expired entries must not appear in assembled prompts.

00:01:21.804 --> 00:01:24.691
Recheck source data before a state-changing action.

00:01:24.841 --> 00:01:30.050
A deletion request must cover indexes, summaries, and backups according to the

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.352
chosen retention policy.

00:01:31.502 --> 00:01:32.173
Question.

00:01:32.323 --> 00:01:34.949
Why not save the entire transcript forever?

00:01:35.099 --> 00:01:35.676
Answer.

00:01:35.826 --> 00:01:41.558
It increases cost, privacy exposure, stale instructions, and irrelevant context.

00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:42.380
Question.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.363
Can a model-generated summary authorize a payment?

00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:46.089
Answer.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:46.723
No.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:51.404
Authorization must refer to exact trusted state and the specific permitted action.
